<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="generator" content="qpcr-assay-check {{ r.tool.version }}">
<title>{{ assay.assay_name }} – assay evaluation record ({{ r.overall.verdict.value }})</title>
<style>
:root {
  --ink: #17222D; --muted: #55636F; --paper: #F4F6F8; --panel: #FFFFFF; --rule: #D3DBE2;
  --pass: #1F7A5A; --pass-bg: #DDF0E7;
  --warn: #9A5F00; --warn-bg: #FBEBC8;
  --fail: #B23B3B; --fail-bg: #F6D9D9;
  --incomplete: #46566B; --incomplete-bg: #DCE2EA;
  --info: #55636F; --info-bg: #E6EAEE;
  --serif: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, Georgia, serif;
  --sans: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { background: var(--paper); }
body { margin: 0; color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; }
main { max-width: 64rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
h1, h2, h3, table, .chip, .meta, .rec { font-family: var(--sans); }
h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 .35rem; }
h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 3rem 0 .75rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 .5rem; }
p { margin: .6rem 0; max-width: 46rem; }
.meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }
.meta code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .8rem; word-break: break-all; }

.verdict { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 0 2rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
  background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-left-width: 10px; padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem; }
.verdict.v-PASS { border-left-color: var(--pass); }
.verdict.v-WARN { border-left-color: var(--warn); }
.verdict.v-FAIL { border-left-color: var(--fail); }
.verdict.v-INCOMPLETE { border-left-color: var(--incomplete); }
.verdict .word { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 2.6rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
.v-PASS .word { color: var(--pass); } .v-WARN .word { color: var(--warn); }
.v-FAIL .word { color: var(--fail); } .v-INCOMPLETE .word { color: var(--incomplete); }
.verdict .label { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: .25rem; }
.verdict ul { margin: .3rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
.verdict li { margin: .2rem 0; }
@media (max-width: 40rem) { .verdict { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem 0; } }

.chip { display: inline-block; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; padding: .1rem .5rem; border-radius: 3px; white-space: nowrap; }
.s-PASS, .s-evaluated-PASS { background: var(--pass-bg); color: var(--pass); }
.s-WARN { background: var(--warn-bg); color: var(--warn); }
.s-FAIL { background: var(--fail-bg); color: var(--fail); }
.s-INFO, .s-none { background: var(--info-bg); color: var(--info); }
.s-INCOMPLETE { background: var(--incomplete-bg); color: var(--incomplete); }

table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .88rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: .45rem .65rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align: top; }
thead th { background: #EAEFF3; font-weight: 600; }
tr.group th { background: #F1F4F7; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
td.num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
.nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
details.more { display: inline; } details.more summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); display: inline; }
td.note { color: var(--muted); }
.scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
.seq { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .92rem; letter-spacing: .04em; word-break: break-all; }
.seq .tail { font-weight: 700; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
pre { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .78rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  padding: .75rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto; line-height: 1.35; }
details { margin: .75rem 0; }
summary { cursor: pointer; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: .9rem; }
summary:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #3B5B7A; outline-offset: 2px; }
a[href^="https://www.ncbi"] { color: #2A5B8A; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
figure { margin: 1rem 0; } figcaption { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); font-family: var(--sans); }
.notice { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: .9rem 1.1rem; }
.notice p { margin: .35rem 0; }
footer { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }

@media print {
  html { background: #fff; } main { max-width: none; padding: 0; }
  .verdict, table, pre, figure, .notice { break-inside: avoid; }
  h2 { break-after: avoid; } details:not([open]) > *:not(summary) { display: block; }
}
.s-critical, .s-likely_detected { background: var(--fail-bg); color: var(--fail); }
.s-warning, .s-amplified_not_detected { background: var(--warn-bg); color: var(--warn); }
.s-minor { background: var(--info-bg); color: var(--info); }
pre.aln { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .78rem; line-height: 1.3; margin: .2rem 0 0; padding: 0; border: 0; background: none; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre; }
.aln .mm { background: var(--fail-bg); color: var(--fail); font-weight: 700; }
.aln .gp { background: var(--warn-bg); }
.aln .un { color: var(--muted); }
.aln .tail { text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
td.aln-cell { min-width: 22rem; }
</style>
{% if plotly_js %}<script>{{ plotly_js }}</script>{% endif %}
</head>
<body>
<main>
{% macro chip(status) %}<span class="chip s-{{ status }}">{{ status }}</span>{% endmacro %}
{% macro match(row, primer) %}{% if row.grade %}<span class="chip {{ grade_css(row.grade) }}" title="{{ row.grade_note }}">{{ row.grade | replace('_', ' ') }}</span><br>{% endif %}{% if row.note %}<strong>{{ row.note }}</strong><br>{% endif %}{% if row.n_mismatch == 0 and row.n_gap == 0 %}perfect match{% else %}{{ row.n_mismatch }} mismatch{{ 'es' if row.n_mismatch != 1 }}{% if row.n_gap %}, {{ row.n_gap }} gap{{ 's' if row.n_gap != 1 }}{% endif %}{% if primer %}<br><span class="meta">{% if row.clean_3prime_nt >= 5 %}3′ end intact ({{ row.clean_3prime_nt }} matching nt){% else %}<strong>mismatch in the 3′ end</strong> ({{ row.clean_3prime_nt }} matching nt){% endif %}</span>{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro grade_css(g) %}{{ {'perfect': 's-PASS', 'tolerated': 's-PASS', 'at_risk': 's-WARN', 'likely_failure': 's-FAIL', 'indeterminate': 's-INCOMPLETE'}.get(g, 's-INFO') }}{% endmacro %}
{% macro pct(value) %}{% if 0 < value < 0.05 %}&lt;0.1%{% else %}{{ '%.1f' % value }}%{% endif %}{% endmacro %}

<header>
  <h1>{{ assay.assay_name }}</h1>
  <p class="meta">
    Assay evaluation record · generated {{ r.generated_at }} · qpcr-assay-check v{{ r.tool.version }} ·
    run <code>{{ r.run_id }}</code><br>
    Inputs hash (SHA-256): <code>{{ r.inputs_hash }}</code>
  </p>
</header>

<section class="verdict v-{{ r.overall.verdict.value }}" aria-labelledby="verdict-h">
  <div>
    <div class="label" id="verdict-h">Overall verdict{% if r.mode == 'qc-only' %} (oligo QC only){% endif %}</div>
    <div class="word">{{ r.overall.verdict.value }}</div>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p>{{ verdict_meaning }}</p>
    {% if r.overall.rationale %}
    <ul>
      {% for line in r.overall.rationale %}<li>{{ line | ncbi }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>

<h2>Sections evaluated</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Result</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for s in r.sections %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ s.title }}</td>
    <td>{% if s.verdict %}{{ chip(s.verdict.value) }}{% else %}<span class="chip s-none">Not evaluated</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="note">{{ s.note | ncbi }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">{% if r.network_used %}This run sent the oligo sequences to NCBI (see Methods).{% else %}No sequence was searched against any database in this run, and no data was sent to NCBI.{% endif %}</p>

<h2>Assay as evaluated</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <tbody>
    {% set kinds = {'forward': 'Forward primer', 'reverse': 'Reverse primer', 'probe': 'Probe'} %}
    {% for o in assay.oligo_list %}
    <tr><th scope="row">{{ kinds[o.role] }}{% if o.name != o.role %} <span class="meta">{{ o.name }}</span>{% endif %}</th>
      <td>{{ o.sequence | seq_html(0 if o.role == 'probe' else 5) }} <span class="meta">{{ o.sequence | length }} nt</span>
      {% if o.role == 'probe' %}<br><span class="meta">reporter {{ o.reporter or 'not specified' }} / quencher {{ o.quencher or 'not specified' }}; modifications: {{ o.modifications | join(', ') or 'none declared' }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    {% if assay.multi_oligo %}<tr><th scope="row">Reaction mix</th><td>Oligos of the same role are alternatives in the same mix: for each record the best-binding one counts. Probes with the same reporter are alternatives; probes with different reporters detect different regions.</td></tr>{% endif %}
    <tr><th scope="row">Template</th><td>{{ assay.template_type.value }}{% if assay.template_type.value == 'RNA' %} (reverse transcription step assumed){% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Intended target</th><td>
      {% if assay.target.taxid %}taxonomy ID {{ assay.target.taxid | taxon }}{% endif %}
      {% if assay.target.accession %}{% if assay.target.taxid %}; {% endif %}reference {{ assay.target.accession | ncbi }}{% endif %}
      {% if assay.target.gene %}; gene {{ assay.target.gene }}{% endif %}
      {% if assay.target.taxa %}<br><strong>Excluding</strong> these taxa and their descendants from the target (left out of the target search, inclusivity and the variant analysis; records of such organisms filed under another taxon, e.g. an unclassified one, stay in the target):
      {% set mnd = assay.target.taxa | selectattr('role', 'equalto', 'must_not_detect') | list %}{% set oos = assay.target.taxa | selectattr('role', 'equalto', 'out_of_scope') | list %}
      {% if mnd %}<br><em>Must not detect</em> ({{ mnd | length }}; searched as near neighbours, part of the specificity verdict): {% for x in mnd %}{{ x.taxid | taxon }}{% if x.reason %} ({{ x.reason }}){% endif %}{{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
      {% if oos %}<br><em>Out of scope</em> ({{ oos | length }}; searched and listed as "also detects", information only, not part of the verdict): {% for x in oos %}{{ x.taxid | taxon }}{% if x.reason %} ({{ x.reason }}){% endif %}{{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% if assay.oligo_source %}<tr><th scope="row">Oligo source</th><td>{{ assay.oligo_source }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if assay.notes %}<tr><th scope="row">Notes</th><td>{{ assay.notes | ncbi }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">The last five nucleotides of each primer, the 3′ end the polymerase extends, are underlined. The probe is not extended, so it has no underline.</p>
{% set degenerate = qc.oligos | selectattr('degenerate') | list %}
{% if degenerate %}
<p>Degenerate oligos were expanded and every variant was evaluated; the worst variant decides each status:
  {% for o in degenerate %}{{ o.role }} → {{ o.n_variants }} variants{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Oligo quality control</h2>
{% if qc.tm_unreliable_reasons %}
<div class="notice"><p><strong>Tm reliability.</strong> The probe carries {{ qc.tm_unreliable_reasons | join(', ') }}.
  Nearest-neighbour Tm and dimer estimates do not model these modifications; use vendor-specific values.</p></div>
{% endif %}
{% for c in charts %}
<figure>
  {{ c.html }}
  <figcaption>{{ c.caption }}</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endfor %}
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Value</th><th>Result</th><th>Rule applied</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for title, items in groups %}
    <tr class="group"><th colspan="4">{{ title }}</th></tr>
    {% for c in items %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ c.name }}{% if c.message %}<br><span class="meta">{{ c.message }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ c.display }}{% if c.unit %} {{ c.unit }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{{ chip(c.status.value) }}</td>
      <td class="note">{{ c.rule }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% if qc.amplicon_note %}<p class="meta">{{ qc.amplicon_note }}</p>{% endif %}

<h2>Hairpins and dimers</h2>
<p>Calculated at the annealing temperature of {{ r.config.reaction.annealing_temp_C }} °C
  (Na⁺ {{ r.config.reaction.na_mM }} mM, Mg²⁺ {{ r.config.reaction.mg_mM }} mM, dNTP {{ r.config.reaction.dntp_mM }} mM).
  A structure is flagged when its melting temperature reaches
  {{ r.config.thresholds.structures.warn_tm_c }} °C (WARN) or the
  {% if r.config.thresholds.structures.fail_tm_c is none %}annealing temperature{% else %}{{ r.config.thresholds.structures.fail_tm_c }} °C{% endif %} (FAIL).
  “3′ end” rows test whether the 3′ end of the first oligo can anneal to the second and be extended.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Structure</th><th>Tm (°C)</th><th>ΔG (kcal/mol)</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for s in qc.structures %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ s.label }}{% if s.n_total > s.n_evaluated %}<br><span class="meta">{{ s.n_evaluated }} of {{ s.n_total }} variant combinations evaluated</span>{% endif %}
      {% if s.variant %}<br><span class="meta">worst case: {{ s.variant }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ s.tm_c | tm }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ s.dg_kcal | dg }}</td>
    <td>{{ chip(s.status.value) }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% if s.ascii_lines %}<tr><td colspan="4"><pre>{{ s.ascii_lines | join('\n') }}</pre></td></tr>{% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">Tm “none” means no structure was found; “&lt; 0” means the only structure is far too weak to matter.
  Thermodynamic values are estimates from primer3 nearest-neighbour parameters.</p>

{% if qc.amplicon %}
<h2>Amplicon</h2>
{% set a = qc.amplicon %}
<div class="scroll"><table><tbody>
  {% if assay.reference_amplicons | length > 1 %}
  <tr><th scope="row">Reference amplicons</th><td>{% for ref in assay.reference_amplicons %}{{ ref.name }} ({{ ref.sequence | length }} nt){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}<br><span class="meta">Each oligo is placed in the reference it fits best (see the checks above); the rows below describe {{ assay.reference_amplicons[0].name }}.</span></td></tr>
  {% else %}
  <tr><th scope="row">Reference amplicon</th><td>{{ a.input_length_nt }} nt</td></tr>
  {% endif %}
  {% if a.product_length_nt %}<tr><th scope="row">Primer-defined product</th><td>{{ a.product_length_nt }} bp, {{ '%.1f' % a.product_gc_percent }}% GC</td></tr>{% endif %}
  {% for site in [a.forward_site, a.reverse_site, a.probe_site] if site %}
  <tr><th scope="row">{{ site.oligo | capitalize if site.oligo in ('forward', 'reverse', 'probe') else site.oligo }} site</th><td>{{ site.start }}–{{ site.end }} ({{ site.strand }}), {{ site.mismatches }} mismatch(es)</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
{% endif %}

{% if spec %}
<h2>Specificity</h2>
<p>{{ chip(spec.verdict_sites.value) }} off-target primer and probe sites &nbsp; {{ chip(spec.verdict_amplicons.value) }} predicted off-target products</p>
<div class="notice"><p><strong>Scope.</strong> {{ spec.scope }} This verdict covers only what was searched and says nothing about organisms outside those tiers.</p></div>

<h3>Rationale</h3>
<ul>
{% for f in spec.findings %}
  <li>{{ chip(f.severity) }} {{ f.message }}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>

<h3>Searches</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Taxa (NCBI taxonomy ID)</th><th>Searches</th><th>Hits per query</th><th>Hit list saturated</th><th>RIDs</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for t in search_rows %}
  <tr><td>{{ t.tier }}</td><td>{{ t.taxids[:5] | map('taxon') | join(', ') }}{% if t.taxids | length > 5 %} <details class="more"><summary>+{{ t.taxids | length - 5 }} more</summary>{{ t.taxids[5:] | map('taxon') | join(', ') }}</details>{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ t.n }}</td>
    <td>{% for k, v in t.hits.items() %}<span class="nowrap">{{ k }}: {{ v }}</span>{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
    <td>{% if t.saturated %}{{ chip('INCOMPLETE') }} {{ t.saturated | join(', ') }}{% else %}no{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ t.rids | join(', ') }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Query</th><th>BLAST hits</th><th>Relevant alignments</th><th>Assessed</th><th>Cut by cap</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for c in spec.counts %}
  <tr><td>{{ c.tier }}</td><td>{{ c.query }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.blast_hits }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.hsps_relevant }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.sites_assessed }}</td><td>{{ 'yes' if c.truncated else 'no' }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">Sites found: {{ spec.n_sites.critical }} critical, {{ spec.n_sites.warning }} warning, {{ spec.n_sites.minor }} minor.
  Levels follow the configured limits (mismatches, gaps and clean 3′ nucleotides). {{ spec.n_fetched }} sequence windows were used for full-length
  re-alignment{% if spec.n_fetch_failed %}; {{ spec.n_fetch_failed }} could not be fetched{% endif %}.</p>

<h2>Predicted off-target products</h2>
{% macro product_table(groups) %}<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Species</th><th>Products</th><th>Probe signal</th><th>Closest product</th><th>Length</th><th>Primer pairs</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for g in groups %}
  <tr><td>{{ g.tier }}</td><td>{{ g.species }}{% if g.names | length > 1 %}<br><span class="meta">{% for n, c in g.names.most_common(3) %}{{ n }} ({{ c }}){{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}{% if g.names | length > 3 %} and {{ g.names | length - 3 }} more{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ g.n_products }}<br><span class="meta">{{ g.n_records }} record{{ '' if g.n_records == 1 else 's' }}</span></td>
    <td>{% if g.n_detected %}{{ chip('likely_detected') }} {{ g.n_detected }}{% endif %}{% if g.n_products - g.n_detected %}{% if g.n_detected %}<br>{% endif %}{{ chip('amplified_not_detected') }} {{ g.n_products - g.n_detected }}{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{{ g.best_mismatches }} primer mismatch{{ '' if g.best_mismatches == 1 else 'es' }}<br><span class="meta">{{ g.best.accession | ncbi }} {{ g.best.start }}–{{ g.best.end }}</span></td>
    <td class="num">{{ g.length_range }}</td><td>{% for pair, c in g.pairs.most_common(3) %}{{ pair }}{% if g.pairs | length > 1 %} ({{ c }}){% endif %}{{ '<br>' | safe if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>{% endmacro %}
{% if spec.amplicons %}
{% set judged = product_groups | rejectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'out_of_scope') | list %}
{% set oos = product_groups | selectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'out_of_scope') | list %}
<p class="meta">One row per search tier and species (identical products counted once), most concerning first: products the probe would detect, then the fewest primer mismatches. Every product is listed in the workbook (sheet "Predicted products"). A product is predicted when two primer sites of at least warning level face each other on the same record within {{ r.config.specificity.max_amplicon_size }} bp; {{ spec.n_primer_only }} primer site(s) at warning or critical level formed no product.</p>
{% if judged %}{% set must = judged | selectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'near_neighbours') | list %}{{ product_table(must + (judged | rejectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'near_neighbours') | list)[:rows_shown]) }}{% if (judged | length) - (must | length) > rows_shown %}<p class="meta">{{ (judged | length) - (must | length) - rows_shown }} further species row(s): see the workbook.</p>{% endif %}
{% else %}<p>No product was predicted in the judged tiers ({{ spec.off_target_tiers_seen | default([]) | join(', ') or 'near neighbours, background, exclusivity' }}).</p>{% endif %}
{% if assay.target.must_not_detect_taxids and not (judged | selectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'near_neighbours') | list) %}<p><strong>No product predicted in the taxa the assay must not detect</strong> ({{ assay.target.must_not_detect_taxids | length }} taxa, searched as near neighbours).</p>{% endif %}
{% if oos %}<details><summary><strong>Also detects (out of scope, information only):</strong> {{ oos | sum(attribute='n_products') }} product(s) in {{ oos | length }} species</summary>
<p class="meta">Taxa the assay is allowed to detect but that are not its intended target (<code>target.taxa</code> with role out_of_scope); not part of the specificity verdict.</p>
{{ product_table(oos) }}</details>{% endif %}
{% else %}
<p>No product was predicted from primer sites of at least warning level in the searched tiers.</p>
{% if assay.target.must_not_detect_taxids %}<p><strong>No product predicted in the taxa the assay must not detect</strong> ({{ assay.target.must_not_detect_taxids | length }} taxa, searched as near neighbours).</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if r.variant_summary and ((r.variant_summary.oligos | selectattr('rows') | list) or r.variant_summary.coverage) %}
<h2>Variant summary (assay's own target)</h2>
{% set cov = r.variant_summary.coverage %}
{% if cov %}
{% if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' %}<div class="notice"><p><strong>Scope: every NCBI Nucleotide record{% if not cov.complete %} assessed so far{% endif %}.</strong> Built from the Nucleotide records of the target (taxonomy ID {{ cov.taxon }}{% if cov.filters.excluded_taxids %}, excluding {{ cov.filters.excluded_taxids }}{% endif %}){% if cov.filters.nucleotide_query %}, narrowed by <code>{{ cov.filters.nucleotide_query }}</code>{% endif %}, newest publication year first. The {{ cov.amplicon_length }} bp reference amplicon ({{ cov.amplicon_source }}) was BLASTed against lists of at most {{ r.config.variants.blast_records_per_search }} of these records at a time, so no search could fill its hit list; hits outside each list were ignored, and partial hits were completed from the record itself. These are counts over all assessed records, not a sample. A record without the region is usually a different gene or a partial sequence, not a missing target.</p></div>
{% else %}<div class="notice"><p><strong>Scope: every genome assembly{% if not cov.complete %} assessed so far{% endif %}.</strong> Built from the genome assemblies of the target (taxonomy ID {{ cov.taxon }}) in NCBI Datasets: current versions{% if cov.filters.exclude_atypical %}, atypical assemblies excluded{% endif %}, one copy per GenBank/RefSeq pair. Each genome was scanned for the {{ cov.amplicon_length }} bp reference amplicon ({{ cov.amplicon_source }}); the oligos were re-aligned end to end in the best complete copy. These are counts over all assessed assemblies, not a sample. Sequences submitted without a genome assembly (single genes, amplicons) are not part of this collection.</p></div>{% endif %}
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <tbody>
  <tr><th scope="row">{{ 'Records' if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' else 'Assemblies' }} listed</th><td>{{ cov.listed_total }} (listed {{ cov.listed_at }})</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Assessed</th><td>{{ cov.assessed_total }}{% if not cov.complete %} &mdash; <strong>incomplete</strong>: at most {{ cov.budget_per_run }} new {{ 'records' if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' else 'assemblies' }} are processed per run, newest first; run again to continue{% endif %}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Processed in this run</th><td>{{ cov.processed_this_run }}{% if cov.download_failed_this_run %}; {{ cov.download_failed_this_run }} download(s) failed and will be retried next run{% endif %}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Amplicon region found</th><td>{{ cov.found }} with all three oligo sites complete</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Region cut by a {{ 'record' if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' else 'contig' }} end</th><td>{{ cov.contig_break }} ({{ 'the record ends inside the amplicon' if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' else 'draft assemblies' }}; not counted in the tables)</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Region hidden by N</th><td>{{ cov.masked }}{% if cov.masked_examples %}<br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ cov.masked_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}<br><span class="meta">The region is there, but the whole region or an oligo site in it reads N (low-coverage sequencing): not counted in the tables, since an N is neither a match nor a variant. A region that is N from end to end is placed by the reference sequence on either side of the amplicon (from the assay's target accession).</span></td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Region not found</th><td>{{ cov.not_found }}{% if cov.not_found_examples %}<br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ cov.not_found_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}<br><span class="meta">No exact {{ r.config.variants.seed_length }}-base stretch of the amplicon anywhere in the {{ 'record' if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' else 'genome' }}: the target region may be absent, or too divergent to find. Where the reference sequence around the amplicon was found, the region there reads real bases, not N; without a target accession in the assay, a region wholly hidden by N is also counted here.</span>
    {% if cov.plasmid_info_recorded and not cov.target_on_plasmid %}<br>of which {{ cov.not_found_without_plasmid }} contain no sequence labelled as a plasmid and {{ cov.not_found_with_plasmid }} contain plasmid sequence{% if cov.target_on_plasmid is none %} (whether the target lies on a plasmid is not known yet){% endif %}.{% endif %}
    {% if cov.target_on_plasmid %}<br>of which <strong>{{ cov.not_found_without_plasmid }}</strong> contain no sequence labelled as a plasmid (many assemblies hold only the chromosome, which says nothing about the strain; in a draft assembly a plasmid can also sit in an unlabelled contig, so a deletion there would be counted here), and <strong>{{ cov.not_found_with_plasmid }}</strong> contain a sequence labelled as a plasmid but not the target region{% if cov.not_found_with_plasmid %} &mdash; <strong>review these</strong>: a possible deletion the assay would miss (as with the Swedish nvCT variant), or an incomplete plasmid assembly: {{ cov.not_found_with_plasmid_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}{% endif %}.{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% if cov.target_on_plasmid is not none %}<tr><th scope="row">Target on a plasmid</th><td>{{ 'yes' if cov.target_on_plasmid else 'no' }} (where the region was found, it lies on a sequence whose description {{ 'names' if cov.target_on_plasmid else 'does not name' }} a plasmid){% if cov.plasmid_header_examples %}<br><span class="meta">Recognised as plasmid, e.g.: {{ cov.plasmid_header_examples[:3] | join('; ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endif %}
  {% if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' %}<tr><th scope="row">How records were checked</th><td>{{ cov.found_by_direct_scan }} with the region found by fetching and scanning the record itself (records up to {{ r.config.variants.direct_scan_max_length }} bases); longer records by BLAST in accession lists{% if cov.not_checked_directly %}<br><strong>{{ cov.not_checked_directly }}</strong> longer record(s) had no BLAST hit and were not scanned directly: their "not found" rests on BLAST alone{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endif %}
  <tr><th scope="row">More than one copy</th><td>{{ cov.multi_copy }} (each genome is judged by the copy the assay binds best; see below)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% set cc = cov.copies %}
{% if cc and cc.genomes %}
<h3>Copies, coverage per oligo, and escapes</h3>
<p class="meta">Every stored copy of the region is assessed with every oligo of the mix. A site is <em>detectable</em> when its graded mismatch class is <em>perfect</em> or <em>tolerated</em> (see "Mismatch classes" under Inclusivity; primers: Stadhouders 2010 and Lefever 2013; probes: at most 1 mismatch outside the last 5 nucleotides, and none for MGB probes){% if cc.homopolymer_bulges_detectable %}, or with no mismatch and only a gap from a single-base run of another length (a homopolymer bulge, e.g. poly-A 7&rarr;8; setting <code>variants.homopolymer_bulges_detectable: true</code>){% else %}; a homopolymer bulge (a single-base run of another length, e.g. poly-A 7&rarr;8) is a gap and is <strong>not</strong> counted as detectable (strict; setting <code>variants.homopolymer_bulges_detectable: false</code>){% endif %}; a copy is detectable when every role is; each genome is judged by its best copy, as the PCR needs only one copy it can amplify. The variant tables below use that best copy.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><tbody>
  <tr><th scope="row">Genomes assessed</th><td>{{ cc.genomes }}; {{ cc.multi_copy }} with more than one copy (at most {{ cc.max_copies }}){% if cc.copies_capped %}<br><span class="meta">{{ cc.copies_capped }} stored before v1.3.0 with at most 5 of their copies; they are downloaded and scanned again on the next runs (within the per-run maximum), so all copies are assessed.</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Best copy not the first found</th><td>{{ cc.best_copy_not_first }}<br><span class="meta">genomes whose best-binding copy differs from the copy found most confidently (earlier versions assessed only that one)</span></td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">With a detectable copy</th><td>{{ cc.with_detectable_copy }} of {{ cc.genomes }} ({{ pct(100.0 * cc.with_detectable_copy / cc.genomes) }}; homopolymer bulges {{ 'counted as detectable' if cc.homopolymer_bulges_detectable else 'not counted (strict)' }})<br><span class="meta">Under both rules: {{ cc.with_detectable_copy_strict }} ({{ pct(100.0 * cc.with_detectable_copy_strict / cc.genomes) }}) strict; {{ cc.with_detectable_copy_bulges }} ({{ pct(100.0 * cc.with_detectable_copy_bulges / cc.genomes) }}) if homopolymer bulges are tolerated. Whether a bulge is amplified or detected is not known from sequence alone; a wet-lab check decides.</span></td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Escapes</strong></th><td><strong>{{ cc.escapes }}</strong> genome(s) without a detectable copy{% if cc.escape_examples %}<br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ cc.escape_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% if cc.undetermined %}<tr><th scope="row">Undetermined</th><td>{{ cc.undetermined }} genome(s) without a detectable copy whose only problem has no published basis: a single mismatch in an MGB probe, or an ambiguity code in the genome near a 3′ end. Counted neither as detected nor as an escape; a wet-lab check decides.{% if cc.undetermined_examples %}<br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ cc.undetermined_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endif %}
</tbody></table></div>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Oligo</th><th>Covers (best copy)</th><th>Only this oligo</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for role in ['forward', 'reverse', 'probe'] %}
  {% for o in cc.oligos if o.role == role %}
  <tr><td>{{ role }}</td><td>{{ o.name }}{% if o.reporter %} <span class="meta">{{ o.reporter }}</span>{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ o.covered }} ({{ pct(100.0 * o.covered / cc.genomes) }})</td><td class="num">{% if assay.by_role(role) | length > 1 %}{{ o.only }}{% else %}–{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  {% if cc.role_undetermined.get(role) %}<tr><td>{{ role }}</td><td><em>undetermined</em></td><td class="num">{{ cc.role_undetermined[role] }}</td><td></td></tr>{% endif %}
  <tr><td>{{ role }}</td><td><em>none of them</em></td><td class="num"><strong>{{ cc.role_none[role] }}</strong>{% if cc.role_none_examples[role] %}<br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ cc.role_none_examples[role][:5] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}</td><td></td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% if cc.channels | length > 1 %}
<p><strong>Probe channels</strong> (probes with different reporters detect different regions; counted as detected when <strong>{{ 'any channel' if cc.probe_channels == 'any' else 'every channel' }}</strong> detects, setting <code>variants.probe_channels</code>):</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Reporter</th><th>Probes</th><th>Genomes detected</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for ch in cc.channels %}<tr><td>{{ ch.reporter }}</td><td>{{ ch.probes | join(', ') }}</td><td class="num">{{ ch.covered }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  <tr><td colspan="2">any channel</td><td class="num">{{ cc.any_channel }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td colspan="2">all channels</td><td class="num">{{ cc.all_channels }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% else %}
<div class="notice"><p><strong>Scope.</strong> Built from the target tier's own BLAST hits: at most {{ r.config.search.hitlist_size }} per oligo, the closest site per record, with partial hits fetched and re-aligned across the whole oligo. Identical alignments are lumped together and each is reported as a percentage of that measured total. When the hit list is full (see Searches) this is BLAST's selection of records, not the whole target population and not a random sample; see Inclusivity below for the year-by-year view against population counts.</p></div>
{% endif %}
{% if r.variant_summary.target_list_full %}<div class="notice"><p><strong>Biased toward perfect matches.</strong> {{ list_full_note }}</p></div>{% endif %}

{% for o in r.variant_summary.oligos %}
{% if o.rows %}
{% set alts = assay.by_role(o.role) %}
<h3>{{ o.role | capitalize }}{% if alts | length > 1 %} <span class="meta">({{ alts | map(attribute='name') | join(', ') }}: for each record the best-binding one is shown)</span>{% elif alts[0].name != o.role %} <span class="meta">{{ alts[0].name }}</span>{% endif %}</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Count</th><th>Fraction</th><th>Match to the oligo</th><th>Example</th>{% if cov %}<th>First / last release</th>{% endif %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% set rare = o.rows | selectattr('percent', 'lt', rare_below) | selectattr('grade', 'in', ['perfect', 'tolerated']) | list %}{% set shown = o.rows | reject('in', rare) | list %}
  {% for row in shown %}
  <tr><td class="aln-cell">{{ row | aln_html(0 if o.role == 'probe' else 5) }}</td><td class="num">{{ row.count }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ pct(row.percent) }} of {{ o.total_measured }}</td>
    <td>{% if alts | length > 1 %}<strong>{{ row.oligo_name }}</strong>: {% endif %}{{ match(row, o.role != 'probe') }}</td>
    <td>{{ row.example_accession | ncbi }}{% if row.example_organism %}<br><span class="meta">{{ row.example_organism }}</span>{% endif %}</td>{% if cov %}<td>{{ row.first_seen or '' }}<br><span class="meta">{{ row.last_seen or '' }}</span></td>{% endif %}</tr>
  {% endfor %}
  {% if rare %}{% set n_rare = rare | sum(attribute='count') %}
  <tr class="group"><td colspan="{{ 6 if cov else 5 }}"><strong>{{ rare | length }} other variant{{ '' if rare | length == 1 else 's' }}</strong>, each seen in fewer than {{ rare_below }}% of records and all perfect or tolerated: {{ n_rare }} record{{ '' if n_rare == 1 else 's' }} ({{ pct(100.0 * n_rare / o.total_measured) }}). Rare variants at risk, likely to fail or indeterminate are always listed above. All variants are in the workbook (sheet "Oligo variants").</td></tr>
  {% endif %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% if o.n_excluded_unmeasured %}<p class="meta">{{ o.n_excluded_unmeasured }} further target-tier site(s) for this oligo excluded from this table: not fully re-aligned (worst-case estimate only).</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if not (r.variant_summary.oligos | selectattr('rows') | list) %}<p><strong>No oligo site could be assessed</strong>: the target region was not found in any assessed record (see the coverage above).</p>{% endif %}
<h3>Whole fragment (forward + probe + reverse combined)</h3>
{% if r.variant_summary.fragments %}
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Forward</th><th>Probe</th><th>Reverse</th><th>Count</th><th>Fraction</th><th>Mismatches (F / P / R)</th><th>Example</th>{% if cov %}<th>First / last release</th>{% endif %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% set safe = ['perfect', 'tolerated'] %}{% set frare = [] %}{% for f in r.variant_summary.fragments %}{% if f.percent < rare_below and f.forward.grade in safe and f.probe.grade in safe and f.reverse.grade in safe %}{% set _ = frare.append(f) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  {% for f in r.variant_summary.fragments if f not in frare %}
  <tr><td class="aln-cell">{{ f.forward | aln_html }}</td><td class="aln-cell">{{ f.probe | aln_html(0) }}</td><td class="aln-cell">{{ f.reverse | aln_html }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ f.count }}</td><td class="num">{{ pct(f.percent) }} of {{ r.variant_summary.fragment_total }}</td>
    <td>{{ f.forward.n_mismatch + f.forward.n_gap }} / {{ f.probe.n_mismatch + f.probe.n_gap }} / {{ f.reverse.n_mismatch + f.reverse.n_gap }}</td>
    <td>{{ f.example_accession | ncbi }}{% if f.example_organism %}<br><span class="meta">{{ f.example_organism }}</span>{% endif %}</td>{% if cov %}<td>{{ f.forward.first_seen or '' }}<br><span class="meta">{{ f.forward.last_seen or '' }}</span></td>{% endif %}</tr>
  {% endfor %}
  {% if frare %}{% set n_fr = frare | sum(attribute='count') %}
  <tr class="group"><td colspan="{{ 8 if cov else 7 }}"><strong>{{ frare | length }} other combination{{ '' if frare | length == 1 else 's' }}</strong>, each seen in fewer than {{ rare_below }}% of records with all three sites perfect or tolerated: {{ n_fr }} record{{ '' if n_fr == 1 else 's' }} ({{ pct(100.0 * n_fr / r.variant_summary.fragment_total) }}). All combinations are in the workbook (sheet "Fragment variants").</td></tr>
  {% endif %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% else %}
<p>No target-tier record had all three sites (forward, probe, reverse) fully re-aligned, so no whole-fragment variant table could be built.</p>
{% endif %}
{% if r.variant_summary.fragment_excluded_unmeasured %}<p class="meta">{{ r.variant_summary.fragment_excluded_unmeasured }} further target-tier record(s) excluded from this table: forward, probe or reverse not among that record's hits, or one of the three not fully re-aligned.{% if r.variant_summary.target_list_full %} With a full hit list, each oligo's hits are a separate selection of records, so most records appear in only one or two of the three lists.{% endif %}</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if r.exclusivity %}
<h2>Exclusivity against the clinical organism list</h2>
<p>{{ chip(r.exclusivity.verdict.value) }} exclusivity ({{ r.exclusivity.n_resolved }} of {{ r.exclusivity.n_organisms }} organism-list name(s) resolved to a taxonomy ID)</p>
{% if r.exclusivity.source == 'assay' %}
<div class="notice"><p><strong>Source: this assay's own list.</strong> This run used the <code>exclusivity_organisms</code>
  list from this assay's own <code>assay.yaml</code> (<code>organisms.source: assay</code>, the default, prefers it over the global list
  whenever the assay defines one). It is not itself claimed to be complete — review and edit it like any other assay input.</p></div>
{% else %}
<div class="notice"><p><strong>Source: the global list.</strong> {% if r.exclusivity.source == 'global' %}This run used the shared, global organism list{% else %}The organism list{% endif %} — a starting point the laboratory must review and edit (see the packaged
  <code>data/clinical_organisms.yaml</code> or your own <code>organisms.list_file</code>); it does not claim to be complete for any particular assay. To use a panel tailored to this assay instead, give it its own <code>exclusivity_organisms</code> list in <code>assay.yaml</code> (used automatically under the default <code>organisms.source: assay</code>).</p></div>
{% endif %}
{% if not r.exclusivity.tier_searched %}
<p>The exclusivity tier was not searched in this run (no organism name resolved to a taxonomy ID, or the tier was excluded from this run), so this section is INCOMPLETE.</p>
{% else %}
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Organism</th><th>Resolution</th><th>Taxonomy ID</th><th>Sites</th><th>Best site</th><th>Predicted product</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in r.exclusivity.rows %}
  <tr><td>{{ row.organism }}</td>
    <td>{% if row.resolution == 'resolved' %}resolved{% else %}{{ chip('INCOMPLETE') }} {{ row.resolution }}{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ (row.taxid | taxon) if row.taxid else '–' }}</td>
    {% if row.is_target %}
    <td class="note" colspan="3">assay's own intended target — excluded from this search (a
      match here is expected and is not evidence of cross-reactivity)</td>
    {% else %}
    <td class="num">{{ row.n_sites }}</td>
    <td>{% if row.best_site_level %}{{ chip(row.best_site_level) }} {{ row.best_site_id }}{% else %}none{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{% if row.amplicon_predicted %}{{ chip(row.amplicon_classification) }}{% else %}no{% endif %}</td>
    {% endif %}
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% if r.exclusivity.unresolved %}
<p class="meta">{{ r.exclusivity.unresolved | length }} organism-list name(s) did not resolve to exactly one taxonomy ID and were not searched (never guessed):
  {% for u in r.exclusivity.unresolved %}{{ u.name }} ({{ u.status }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. Review the organism list.</p>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if r.inclusivity %}
{% set nuc = r.inclusivity.exhaustive and r.inclusivity.sample_scheme.startswith('Every NCBI Nucleotide record') %}
<h2>Inclusivity across the intended target ({{ ('all Nucleotide records' if nuc else 'all genome assemblies') if r.inclusivity.exhaustive else 'sampled' }})</h2>
<p>{{ chip(r.inclusivity.verdict.value) }} inclusivity</p>
{% if not r.inclusivity.tier_searched %}
<p>The target tier was not searched in this run, so this section is INCOMPLETE.</p>
{% else %}
<div class="notice"><p><strong>Sampling.</strong> {{ r.inclusivity.sample_scheme }}</p></div>
{% for o in r.inclusivity.oligos %}
<h3>{{ o.role | capitalize }}</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>{{ ('Records' if nuc else 'Assemblies') if r.inclusivity.exhaustive else 'Population' }}</th><th>{{ 'With region' if r.inclusivity.exhaustive else 'Sample' }}</th><th>Perfect</th><th>1 mismatch</th><th>2+ mismatch/gap</th><th>3′ mismatch</th><th>Fetch failed</th>{% if o.windows | rejectattr('n_detectable', 'none') | list %}<th>Detectable</th><th>At risk</th><th>Likely failure</th><th>Indeterminate</th>{% endif %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for w in o.windows %}
  <tr><td class="num">{{ w.year }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.population_size if w.population_size is not none else '–' }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ w.sample_size }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_perfect }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_one_mismatch }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ w.n_two_plus_mismatch }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_three_prime_mismatch }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_fetch_failed }}</td>{% if w.n_detectable is not none %}<td class="num">{{ w.n_detectable }}{% if w.sample_size %} ({{ pct(100.0 * w.n_detectable / w.sample_size) }}){% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_by_grade.get('at_risk', 0) }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_by_grade.get('likely_failure', 0) }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_by_grade.get('indeterminate', 0) }}</td>{% elif o.windows | rejectattr('n_detectable', 'none') | list %}<td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td>{% endif %}</tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% if loop.last and r.inclusivity.oligos | map(attribute='windows') | map('rejectattr', 'n_detectable', 'none') | map('list') | select | list %}
<h3>Mismatch classes</h3>
<p class="meta">Each oligo site on the target gets a class (docs/MISMATCH_CLASSES.md): <em>perfect</em>; <em>tolerated</em> (expected to cost little); <em>at risk</em> (a measurable delay is expected, worse near the limit of detection); <em>likely failure</em> (blocked or strongly delayed in the published data); <em>indeterminate</em> (no published basis: gaps and homopolymer bulges, ambiguity codes in the genome, mismatches in MGB probes). <em>Detectable</em> = perfect or tolerated; the verdict thresholds apply to it. A single mismatch in an MGB probe and an ambiguity code in the genome near a 3′ end are <em>undetermined</em>: left out of the percentage (neither detected nor escaped). Gaps count as not detected (homopolymer bulges: see the setting). Primers: single mismatches in the last 5 nt by type and position after Stadhouders et al., J Mol Diagn 2010 (Table 1, Taq polymerase on DNA); farther positions and the number of mismatches per primer and per primer pair after Lefever et al., Clin Chem 2013. Probes: no published rule was used (at most 1 mismatch outside the last 5 nt is tolerated). {{ grade_caveat }}</p>
{% endif %}
{% if o.n_no_date %}<p class="meta">{{ o.n_no_date }} sampled hit(s) had no determinable submission year and were excluded from the yearly buckets.</p>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if r.inclusivity.rationale %}
<h3>Rationale</h3>
<ul>{% for line in r.inclusivity.rationale %}<li>{{ line | ncbi }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% endif %}
{% if r.inclusivity.limitations %}
<p class="meta">{% for l in r.inclusivity.limitations %}{{ l | ncbi }} {% endfor %}</p>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if r.taxonomy_breakdown %}
<h2>Off-target sites per species</h2>
{% macro site_table(groups) %}<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Species</th><th>Sites</th><th>Critical / warning</th><th>Closest site</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for g in groups %}
  <tr><td>{{ g.tier }}</td><td>{{ g.species }}{% if g.names | length > 1 %}<br><span class="meta">{% for n, c in g.names.most_common(3) %}{{ n }} ({{ c }}){{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}{% if g.names | length > 3 %} and {{ g.names | length - 3 }} more{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ g.n_sites }}<br><span class="meta">{{ g.n_records }} record{{ '' if g.n_records == 1 else 's' }}</span></td>
    <td class="num">{{ g.levels['critical'] }} / {{ g.levels['warning'] }}</td>
    <td>{{ g.best.query }}: {{ g.best.n_mismatch }} mismatch{{ '' if g.best.n_mismatch == 1 else 'es' }}{% if g.best.n_gap %} + {{ g.best.n_gap }} gap{% endif %}, {{ g.best.clean_3prime_nt }} clean 3′ nt<br><span class="meta">{{ g.best.accession | ncbi }}</span></td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>{% endmacro %}
{% if site_groups %}
{% set judged_s = site_groups | rejectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'out_of_scope') | list %}{% set oos_s = site_groups | selectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'out_of_scope') | list %}
<p class="meta">Off-target sites at warning or critical level, one row per search tier and species (species from NCBI Taxonomy lineages), closest first. Every site is in hits.tsv and the workbook (sheets "Off-target sites" and "Taxonomy breakdown").</p>
{% set must_s = judged_s | selectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'near_neighbours') | list %}{{ site_table(must_s + (judged_s | rejectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'near_neighbours') | list)[:rows_shown]) }}
{% if (judged_s | length) - (must_s | length) > rows_shown %}<p class="meta">{{ (judged_s | length) - (must_s | length) - rows_shown }} further species row(s): see the workbook.</p>{% endif %}
{% if oos_s %}<details><summary><strong>Out of scope (information only):</strong> {{ oos_s | sum(attribute='n_sites') }} site(s) in {{ oos_s | length }} species</summary>{{ site_table(oos_s) }}</details>{% endif %}
{% else %}<p>No off-target site at warning or critical level.</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}

<h2>Closest off-target sites</h2>
{% if shown_variants %}
<p class="meta">Off-target sites grouped by oligo and alignment: sites where an oligo aligns identically bind the same way, so each row is one binding variant, with how many sites and records have it and in which organisms.
  Each alignment shows the oligo (top) against the subject (bottom), oriented as the oligo. Highlighted subject bases are mismatches;
  shaded columns are gaps; dots mark bases BLAST left unaligned and that were not re-aligned (worst-case assessment). The primer 3′ end (last 5 nucleotides) is underlined.
  Only the closest (most likely to bind) variants are shown; every single site is in hits.tsv and the workbook's "Off-target sites" sheet.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Oligo</th><th>Alignment</th><th>Mismatches</th><th>Clean 3′</th><th>Duplex</th><th>Sites</th><th>Organisms</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for g in shown_variants %}
  <tr><td>{{ chip(g.level) }}<br><span class="meta">{{ g.tiers | join(', ') }}</span></td><td>{{ g.query }}</td>
    <td class="aln-cell">{{ g.example_site | aln_html }}<span class="meta">{{ {'blast_full': 'BLAST alignment', 'realigned': 'full-length re-alignment', 'blast_partial_worst_case': 'worst case (not re-aligned)'}[g.source] }}</span></td>
    <td class="num">{{ g.n_mismatch }}{% if g.n_gap %} + {{ g.n_gap }} gap{% endif %}{% if g.n_unaligned %}<br><span class="meta">{{ g.n_unaligned }} unaligned</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ g.clean_3prime_nt }}</td>
    <td class="num">{% if g.tm_c is not none %}Tm {{ '%.1f' % g.tm_c }} °C<br><span class="meta">{% if g.delta_tm_c is not none %}{{ '%+.1f' % g.delta_tm_c }} °C vs perfect{% endif %}</span>{% else %}–{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ g.n_sites }}{% if g.n_records != g.n_sites %}<br><span class="meta">{{ g.n_records }} records</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{% for name, n in g.organisms[:5] %}{{ name }}{% if g.organisms | length > 1 %} ({{ n }}){% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if g.organisms | length > 5 %}<br><span class="meta">and {{ g.organisms | length - 5 }} more</span>{% endif %}
      <br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ g.example_site.accession | ncbi }} {{ g.example_site.subject_start }}–{{ g.example_site.subject_end }} ({{ g.example_site.orientation }})</span></td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% if hidden_variants %}<p class="meta">{{ hidden_variants }} further variant(s) ({{ hidden_variant_sites }} site(s)) are listed in hits.tsv and the workbook.</p>{% endif %}
<p class="meta">Duplex Tm is a nearest-neighbour estimate of stability. A mismatch at the 3′-terminal base is treated as an unpaired overhang and barely lowers it,
  although it usually prevents extension: judge priming from the mismatch and 3′ columns, not from Tm.</p>
{% else %}
<p>No site with enough identical bases to be relevant was found in the searched off-target tiers.</p>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if r.history %}
<h2>Changes since the previous run</h2>
{% if not r.history.has_previous %}
<p><span class="chip s-INCOMPLETE">INCOMPLETE</span> This is the first recorded run for this assay: there is nothing yet to compare it against.</p>
{% else %}
<p>{{ chip(r.history.verdict.value) }} compared to the run on {{ r.history.previous_generated_at }}
  (<code>{{ r.history.previous_run_id }}</code>)</p>
{% if r.history.inputs_changed %}<div class="notice"><p>The assay definition or configuration changed since that run: some of the differences below may reflect that rather than new NCBI data.</p></div>{% endif %}
<ul>{% for line in r.history.rationale %}<li>{{ line | ncbi }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% set changed_sections = r.history.section_changes | selectattr('changed') | list %}
{% if changed_sections %}
<h3>Section verdicts</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Before</th><th>After</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for sc in changed_sections %}
  <tr><td>{{ sc.title }}</td>
    <td>{% if sc.verdict_before %}{{ chip(sc.verdict_before.value) }}{% else %}<span class="chip s-none">not evaluated</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{% if sc.verdict_after %}{{ chip(sc.verdict_after.value) }}{% else %}<span class="chip s-none">not evaluated</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}
{% if r.history.new_sites or r.history.resolved_sites or r.history.changed_sites %}
<h3>Off-target sites</h3>
<p class="meta">Matched across runs by accession and position, not by the run-local site ID.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Change</th><th>Tier</th><th>Oligo</th><th>Organism / record</th><th>Position</th><th>Level</th><th>Mismatches</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for s in r.history.new_sites %}
  <tr><td><span class="chip s-WARN">new</span></td><td>{{ s.tier }}</td><td>{{ s.role }}</td>
    <td>{{ s.organism or 'unknown' }}<br><span class="meta">{{ s.accession | ncbi }}</span></td>
    <td class="num">{{ s.subject_start }}–{{ s.subject_end }} ({{ s.orientation }})</td>
    <td>{{ chip(s.level_after) }}</td><td class="num">{{ s.n_mismatch_after }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  {% for s in r.history.resolved_sites %}
  <tr><td><span class="chip s-PASS">resolved</span></td><td>{{ s.tier }}</td><td>{{ s.role }}</td>
    <td>{{ s.organism or 'unknown' }}<br><span class="meta">{{ s.accession | ncbi }}</span></td>
    <td class="num">{{ s.subject_start }}–{{ s.subject_end }} ({{ s.orientation }})</td>
    <td>{{ chip(s.level_before) }}</td><td class="num">{{ s.n_mismatch_before }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  {% for s in r.history.changed_sites %}
  <tr><td><span class="chip s-INFO">changed</span></td><td>{{ s.tier }}</td><td>{{ s.role }}</td>
    <td>{{ s.organism or 'unknown' }}<br><span class="meta">{{ s.accession | ncbi }}</span></td>
    <td class="num">{{ s.subject_start }}–{{ s.subject_end }} ({{ s.orientation }})</td>
    <td>{{ chip(s.level_before) }} → {{ chip(s.level_after) }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ s.n_mismatch_before }} → {{ s.n_mismatch_after }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}
{% if r.history.new_amplicons or r.history.resolved_amplicons %}
<h3>Predicted off-target products</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Change</th><th>Tier</th><th>Organism / record</th><th>Position</th><th>Primers</th><th>Class</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for a in r.history.new_amplicons %}
  <tr><td><span class="chip s-WARN">new</span></td><td>{{ a.tier }}</td>
    <td>{{ a.organism or 'unknown' }}<br><span class="meta">{{ a.accession | ncbi }}</span></td>
    <td class="num">{{ a.start }}–{{ a.end }}</td><td>{{ a.roles }}</td>
    <td>{% if a.classification %}{{ chip(a.classification) }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  {% for a in r.history.resolved_amplicons %}
  <tr><td><span class="chip s-PASS">resolved</span></td><td>{{ a.tier }}</td>
    <td>{{ a.organism or 'unknown' }}<br><span class="meta">{{ a.accession | ncbi }}</span></td>
    <td class="num">{{ a.start }}–{{ a.end }}</td><td>{{ a.roles }}</td>
    <td>{% if a.classification %}{{ chip(a.classification) }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}
{% if r.history.inclusivity_changes %}
<h3>Inclusivity trend</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Oligo</th><th>Year</th><th>Before</th><th>After</th><th>New mismatch position(s)</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for c in r.history.inclusivity_changes %}
  <tr><td>{{ c.role }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.year }}</td>
    <td class="num">{% if c.percent_before is not none %}{{ '%.0f' % c.percent_before }}% of {{ c.sample_size_before }}{% else %}–{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{% if c.percent_after is not none %}{{ '%.0f' % c.percent_after }}% of {{ c.sample_size_after }}{% else %}–{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ c.new_mismatch_positions | join(', ') or '–' }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}
{% if r.history.variant_changes %}
<h3>Oligo sequence variants since the previous run</h3>
<p class="meta">"Emerging": the variant's first record (assembly or Nucleotide record) was released after the previous run. "Newly assessed": it is in an older record that this run assessed for the first time (e.g. the previous run had not finished the collection).</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Change</th><th>Oligo</th><th>Variant</th><th>Match to the oligo</th><th>Records</th><th>First release</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for v in r.history.variant_changes %}
  <tr><td>{% if v.kind == 'new' %}{% if v.concern %}<strong>new</strong>{% else %}new{% endif %}<br><span class="meta">{{ 'emerging' if v.newly_released else ('newly assessed' if v.newly_released is not none else 'release date unknown') }}</span>{% else %}no longer seen{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{{ v.role }}</td>
    <td class="aln-cell">{{ v | aln_html(0 if v.role == 'probe' else 5) }}</td>
    <td>{{ match(v, v.role != 'probe') }}</td>
    <td class="num">{% if v.kind == 'new' %}{{ v.count_after }}{% if v.percent_after is not none %} ({{ pct(v.percent_after) }}){% endif %}{% else %}{{ v.count_before }} before{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{{ v.first_seen or '' }}</td><td>{{ v.example_accession | ncbi }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% elif r.history.variants_note %}
<p class="meta">{{ r.history.variants_note | ncbi }}</p>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if pending %}
<h2>Not yet evaluated</h2>
<div class="notice">
  <p>The following parts of the evaluation were not performed in this record, so the overall verdict cannot be a pass:</p>
  <ul>{% for s in pending %}<li>{{ s.title }}: {{ s.note | ncbi }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>Methods</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table><tbody>
  <tr><th scope="row">Software</th><td>qpcr-assay-check {{ r.tool.version }}; Python {{ r.environment.python }}; primer3-py {{ r.environment['primer3-py'] }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Platform</th><td>{{ r.environment.platform }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Melting temperature</th><td>{{ r.config.reaction.tm_method }} nearest-neighbour model, {{ r.config.reaction.salt_correction }} salt correction;
    primers {{ r.config.reaction.primer_nM }} nM, probe {{ r.config.reaction.probe_nM }} nM</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Structures</th><td>primer3 thermodynamic alignment (hairpin, homodimer, heterodimer, 3′-end) at {{ r.config.reaction.annealing_temp_C }} °C</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">3′ end stability</th><td>Sum of SantaLucia (1998) nearest-neighbour ΔG°37 over the last five nucleotides (informational)</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Run mode</th><td>{{ r.mode }}</td></tr>
  {% if spec %}
  {% set bp = spec.parameters.blast %}
  <tr><th scope="row">Database searched</th><td>{{ spec.parameters.databases | join(', ') or 'not reported' }}; {{ spec.parameters.blast_versions | join(', ') }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">BLAST parameters</th><td>{% for k, v in bp.items() %}{{ k }} = {{ v }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Taxon restriction check</th><td>{% for t in search_rows %}{{ t.tier }}: {{ t.in_requested }} of {{ t.descriptions }} hit descriptions carry a requested taxon ID, {{ t.other }} another (possibly a descendant strain), {{ t.no_taxid }} none{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}<br>
    <span class="meta">The restriction (ENTREZ_QUERY on the organism index) is effective but not airtight. These counts compare exact taxon IDs only; a hit filed under a descendant strain is counted as “another”, since the restriction itself is not checked by lineage.</span></td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Re-alignment</th><td>Semi-global, affine gaps: match {{ spec.parameters.alignment.match }}, mismatch {{ spec.parameters.alignment.mismatch }},
    gap {{ spec.parameters.alignment.gap_open }} + {{ spec.parameters.alignment.gap_extend }} per base; partial hits completed from sequence windows fetched with E-utilities efetch ({{ spec.parameters.window_padding_nt }} nt padding)</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Search and RIDs</th><td>{% for t in search_rows %}{{ t.tier }}: {{ t.rids | join(', ') }}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Data sent to NCBI</th><td>The oligo sequences (forward, reverse, probe and any expanded degenerate variants) and the taxon restrictions above.</td></tr>
  {% else %}
  <tr><th scope="row">Database, BLAST parameters, RIDs</th><td>Not applicable: no database search was performed</td></tr>
  {% endif %}
</tbody></table></div>
{% if assay_settings_yaml %}
<p><strong>Settings from the assay file</strong> (applied over the defaults and any configuration file):</p>
<pre>{{ assay_settings_yaml }}</pre>
{% endif %}
<details>
  <summary>Effective configuration (thresholds and conditions applied)</summary>
  <pre>{{ config_yaml }}</pre>
</details>

<h2>Limitations</h2>
<p>Default thresholds are starting points drawn from common TaqMan design guidance; they are not acceptance
  criteria and must be reviewed by the laboratory. Melting temperatures and dimer energies are computational
  estimates and depend on the reaction conditions entered. Structures are searched at the annealing temperature, so a
  hairpin or dimer that forms only at lower temperatures (for example during reaction set-up) may not be reported, and
  the same oligo can be flagged at one annealing temperature and not at another. Modified probes (MGB, LNA, ZEN and
  similar) are not modelled. These results describe the oligo sequences only: nothing here says how the assay behaves
  against real specimens or real off-target sequences.</p>
{% if spec %}
<ul>{% for text in spec.limitations %}<li>{{ text | ncbi }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% endif %}

<h2>Required statements</h2>
<div class="notice">
  <p><strong>In silico analysis does not replace experimental validation.</strong> The outcome of this evaluation
    must be interpreted together with wet-laboratory verification of the assay.</p>
  <p><strong>The laboratory is responsible for verifying this software within its own quality system</strong>
    before relying on its output. qpcr-assay-check is provided without warranty (Apache License 2.0).</p>
</div>

<footer class="meta">
  Record {{ r.run_id }} · generated {{ r.generated_at }} (UTC) · qpcr-assay-check v{{ r.tool.version }} ·
  inputs hash {{ r.inputs_hash[:16] }}… · schema {{ r.schema_version }}
</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
